statement:
For all P, n ∈ ℕ, U ⊆ ℝ^P, T ∈ 𝒟_n(U), S ∈ 𝒟_n(ℝ^P) (GeometricCurrentOn univ n), z ∈ ℝ^P, reals r, θ₂, ρ₀, points x_i ∈ ℝ^P and reals λ_i > 0 (i ∈ ℕ), assume:
- r > 0, θ₂ ≥ 0, ρ₀ > 0 and B_{2r}(z) ⊆ U;
- M_{B_ρ(y)}(T) ≤ ofReal(θ₂)·ω_n·ofReal(ρ^n) for every y ∈ B_{3r/2}(z) and every ρ with 0 < ρ < ρ₀;
- x_i ∈ B_r(z) for every i, and λ_i → 0;
- blowUp T x_i λ_i ⇀ S (ConvergesWeakly).

Then (1) M_{B_ρ(w)}(S) ≤ ofReal(θ₂)·ω_n·ofReal(ρ^n) for every w ∈ ℝ^P and every ρ > 0; and (2) θ ≤ θ₂ whenever HasMassDensity S w θ (w ∈ ℝ^P, θ ∈ ℝ). Here M_W = massOn, ω_n = unitBallVolume n, ofReal = ENNReal.ofReal, and balls are open.
